.TH "ODIR-SETDEBUG" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-setdebug \- setdebug: Sets debug level
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
setdebug [level=<level>] [trace=<\-1|0|1>] [timestamp=<\-1|0|1>] [hangup=<\-1|0|1>] [tags=<tags>] [client=<client>] [storage=<storage>] [dir] [director] [all]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Sets the debug level of the Director (dir or director), a File Daemon (client=), a Storage Daemon (storage=) or all daemons at once (all). Level 0 switches debug output off. The running daemon is changed, not its configuration; after a restart the start value applies again.
.PP
trace= writes the debug output to a trace file in the working directory, timestamp= prefixes every debug line with a time stamp; without them the setting stays unchanged. hangup= is a File Daemon test aid that drops the connection after n files. A missing level is asked for, a missing target leads to a daemon selection.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "setdebug"
.TP
.B "level=<level>"
Debug level (number)
.TP
.B "trace=<\-1|0|1>"
Trace flag (one of a fixed set; values: \-1, 0, 1)
.TP
.B "timestamp=<\-1|0|1>"
Timestamp flag (one of a fixed set; values: \-1, 0, 1)
.TP
.B "hangup=<\-1|0|1>"
FD hangup flag (one of a fixed set; values: \-1, 0, 1)
.TP
.B "tags=<tags>"
Debug tags (text)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
File Daemon (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage Daemon (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "dir"
The Director (keyword)
.TP
.B "director"
The Director (keyword)
.TP
.B "all"
Every daemon (keyword)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "setdebug level=100 trace=1 dir"
verbose Director debugging into the trace file
.TP
.B "setdebug level=200 timestamp=1 client=bareos\-fd"
debug the File Daemon with time stamps
.TP
.B "setdebug level=0 all"
switch debug output off everywhere
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
